From: Guohan Lu <securely1g@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] Register lazy APT lock-import regression repositories

Expose the reviewed Debian archive fixture to external registry consumers.
The test compares independent runtime/control targets, complete dependency
closures and two isolated imports on native AMD64 and ARM64. Existing archive
inputs are fetched and extracted; no DEB is built.

Origin: tests maintained with the import_lock extension in
securely1g/sonic-build-infra/third_party/rules_distroless.
Signed-off-by: Guohan Lu <securely1g@gmail.com>

--- a/MODULE.bazel
+++ b/MODULE.bazel
@@ -53,3 +53,8 @@
 use_repo(registry_ci, "registry_ci_libpcap_arm64")
 use_repo(registry_ci, "registry_ci_boost_amd64")
 use_repo(registry_ci, "registry_ci_boost_arm64")
+
+# Import existing Debian archives only; these tests never build a DEB.
+locked_apt_ci = use_extension("//apt:extensions.bzl", "apt")
+locked_apt_ci.import_lock(lock = "//registry_ci/locked_import:apt.lock.json")
+use_repo(locked_apt_ci, "locked_import_ci", "locked_import_ci_copy")
